Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- UUX-1-06: ONE shared NORMAL-verb prompt (promptNormalApprovalVerbs) for the
  inline confirm AND the deferred fallback; ToolAction-bound verbs ([p]/[P]/[h])
  are capability-DECLARED, not forked; deferred 't <steer>' now survives as
  {decision:'deny', steer} through the wire union.
- UUX-1-19: attach prompt upgrades y/N → [y]/[a]lways-session/[N]/deny+s[t]eer;
  wire capability verified (ApprovalRespondCommand.scope/steer forwarded by the
  kernel scheduler to host.resolveApproval); rich answer sent verbatim, approve
  re-runs the turn (web parity), legacy string answers byte-identical.
- UUX-2-18: empty deny-steer re-prompts once ('steer text required (or N to
  deny)') in the shared reader — repl inline + deferred + escalation + attach.
- C2: awaitLine(signal?, label?) — a superseded release names its superseder;
  askLine + elicitation reads print WHICH ask won; unlabeled shapes untouched.
- C3 (mitigation): attach ApprovalLineGate orders line ARRIVALS vs prompt
  RENDER — a line typed before the approval prompt appeared flows to the
  session, never eaten as its answer (audit scenario pinned).

Hellgate: RED-first proven (9 verb/steer/label fails + labeled-supersede +
attach export missing), then green; adversarial audit caught a real
return-in-try/finally release-ordering bug (return await, pinned by tests).

